+# OHOS adaptation: the upstream KIO worker (audiocd.cpp) and the KCM settings
+# module (kcmaudiocd/) both depend on KF6::KIO / KF6::KCMUtils / KF6::Solid,
+# none of which are published to the ohpcd conan registry. Additionally the
+# worker's ripping core requires a raw optical drive device (/dev/sr0 style
+# cdda access via cdparanoia), which does not exist on HarmonyOS PC. The
+# reusable deliverable on this platform is therefore the audiocdplugins
+# encoder library plus the encoder plugins themselves (wav/flac/vorbis/lame/
+# opus), which other applications (e.g. KAudioCreator-style rippers) embed
+# directly without a KIO daemon. KIO/KCMUtils/Solid/KCddb worker usage is
+# trimmed from the CMake graph accordingly; the encoder plugin ABI keeps the
+# upstream create_audiocd_encoders symbol with a self-contained data sink
+# interface (audiocdencoder.h) instead of KIO::WorkerBase.
